<article class="env-lemma" id="0H0N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H0N">Lemma <span data-tag="0H0N">13.40.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a triangulated category. Let $\mathcal{B}$ be a full triangulated subcategory of $\mathcal{D}$. For an object $X$ of $\mathcal{D}$ consider the property $P(X)$: there exists a distinguished triangle $A \to X \to B \to A[1]$ in $\mathcal{D}$ with $B$ in $\mathcal{B}$ and $A$ in ${}^\perp \mathcal{B}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $X_1 \to X_2 \to X_3 \to X_1[1]$ is a distinguished triangle and $P$ holds for two out of three, then it holds for the third. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $P$ holds for $X_1$ and $X_2$, then it holds for $X_1 \oplus X_2$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/0CQR" data-tag="0CQR">13.40.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>